</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Implementation details and hyperparameters</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We train all masks using the HuggingFace Trainer API <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wolf et al., 2020</a>)</cite> for 2000 steps with a global batch size of 256 and a sequence length of 4096, resulting in 2B tokens processed from the SlimPajama corpus <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Soboleva et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Training is accelerated via data parallelism across a single node with 4 H100 GPUs. In this setup, <span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PATCH<math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}^{\text{Joint}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>Joint</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{\text{Joint}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> requires 4.5 and 6 GPU hours on the 0.5B and 1B models, respectively, while <span id="A4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PATCH<math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}^{\text{Tile}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>Tile</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{\text{Tile}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> requires 21 and 24 GPU hours on the 7B and 8B models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The hyperparameters for <span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PATCH<math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}^{\text{Joint}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>Joint</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{\text{Joint}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> and <span id="A4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PATCH<math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}^{\text{Tile}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>Tile</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{\text{Tile}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> are summarized in Table <a href="#A4.T15" title="Table 15 ‣ Appendix D Implementation details and hyperparameters ‣ PATCH: Learnable Tile-Level Hybrid Sparsity for LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, tuned on Qwen-2.5-0.5B. For the 2:4 mask parameters, we follow the configuration from MaskLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T15" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 15: </span>Hyper-parameters used for <span id="A4.T15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PATCH<math id="A4.T15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}^{\text{Joint}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>Joint</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{\text{Joint}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> and <span id="A4.T15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PATCH<math id="A4.T15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}^{\text{Tile}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>Tile</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{\text{Tile}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> across sparsity ratios. All hyper parameters were tuned on Qwen-2.5-0.5B.</figcaption>
<div id="A4.T15.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:53.1pt;vertical-align:-25.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-123.0pt,16.4pt) scale(0.617690146498569,0.617690146498569) ;">
